    <statement><p>Consider the cone shown below.</p>
<image xmlns:pi="http://pretextbook.org/2020/pretext/internal" pi:generated="webwork/images/Library__Michigan__Chap17Sec5__Q31__pg-image-1.png" width="38%">
<shortdescription>A plot of a cone surface with vertex on the z-axis</shortdescription>
<description>
<p>figure of a cone with circular base on the xy-plane, centered on the z-axis, and point on the positive z-axis.</p>
</description>
</image>
<p>If the height of the cone is 6 and the base radius is 5, write
a parameterization of the cone in terms of <m>r = s</m> and <m>\theta = t</m>.</p>
<p><m>x(s,t) =</m> <fillin characters="45" name="AnSwEr0001"/>,</p>
<p><m>y(s,t) =</m> <fillin characters="45" name="AnSwEr0002"/>, and</p>
<p><m>z(s,t) =</m> <fillin characters="45" name="AnSwEr0003"/>, with</p>
<p><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/> <m>\le s\le</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0005"/> and</p>
<p><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0006"/> <m>\le t\le</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0007"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>s\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>s\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6-\frac{6}{5}s</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2\pi </m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>r</m> and angle <m>\theta</m>, we find <m>x</m>, <m>y</m> and <m>z</m>
in terms of the parameters <m>r = s</m> and <m>\theta = t</m>.  We have
<me>x = s\cos t,</me>
<me>y = s\sin t,</me>
and
<me>z = 6 ( 1 - \frac{1}{5}\, s ),</me>
with
<me>0 \le s\le 5 \quad\mbox{and}\quad 0\le t\le 2\pi.</me>
There are, of course, other parameterizations, but they will not be
in terms of <m>r</m> and <m>\theta</m>, as required in this problem.



</solution>
